Id: stor005i
Severity: INFO
Category: filesystem
Check: check_storage
References: cryptsetup(8)

Some local file systems are not encrypted (the detail lists them).
Whoever gets hold of the disks, a stolen machine, a disk sent back
under warranty or thrown away, can read them. Whether that matters
depends on where the machine is: for a server in a locked room it may
not, which is why this is informational on a machine without a battery
(stor004w is the warning for portable ones). LUKS is the usual way to
encrypt them.
